v3/program-days.integratorAPI:
No integrator action needed here (my scope never touches App/, Features/Home/ or Features/Settings/). For reference, what changed in the shared protocol:

protocol ProgramRepositoring (Persistence/Repositories/ProgramRepositoring.swift) gained:
  func addDay(programID: UUID, name: String?) throws -> UUID
    // name == nil -> next free "Dia X" (A, B, C...); name != nil -> trimmed literal name.
    // Throws .tooManyDays above ProgramLimits.maxDays (7).
  func removeDay(id: UUID) throws
    // Cascades to ProgramExerciseModel. Throws .tooFewDays below ProgramLimits.minDays (1).
    // Never touches session history (WorkoutSessionModel.programDayName is an independent snapshot).
  func renameDay(id: UUID, to name: String) throws
    // Throws .invalidParameters(...) on blank (whitespace-only) name.
  func moveDay(id: UUID, toIndex newIndex: Int) throws
    // 0-based; renumbers `order` 0...n-1. Throws .invalidParameters on out-of-range index.

All four have default throwing implementations in `extension ProgramRepositoring` (satisfy the protocol for any other conformer without changes); ProgramRepository (real) and the ProgramPreviewRepository double both override with full behavior.

ProgramRepositoryError gained two new cases: .tooManyDays, .tooFewDays (both already wired into the exhaustive switches in ProgramDetailViewModel.message(for:) and ProgramListViewModel.message(for:)).

ProgramLimits gained: static let minDays = 1, static let maxDays = 7.

ProgramDetailViewModel (Features/Program) gained, for anyone building further UI on top of it: var canAddDay: Bool, var canRemoveDay: Bool, func addDay(), func renameDay(id dayID: UUID, to newName: String), func removeDay(id dayID: UUID), func moveDays(fromOffsets:toOffset:). All follow the exact same perform/reload pattern as the existing exercise-target methods.

